205 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (Daniel W. Graham coined the term "hestiocentrism" to describe this system, distinguishing it from both geocentrism and heliocentrism. The central fire does not illuminate: it is simply the focal point around which all celestial bodies orbit. Carl Huffman calls it "speculative astronomy," while Walter Burkert observes that "there is nothing mathematical about Philolaic astronomy.")
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
