/P 103 0 R
/E (The Counter-Earth represents one of the most enigmatic aspects of the Philolaic system. Aristotle suggests it was postulated for numerological reasons: with the Counter-Earth, the total number of celestial bodies reaches the perfect number of ten \(together with the Sun, the Moon, the five planets, the Earth, and the sphere of the fixed stars\). However, the Counter-Earth also carries significant astronomical implications.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
