264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (The history of Pythagorean cosmology, from Pythagoras to Philolaus, represented the first systematic Western attempt to provide a quantitative and mathematical interpretation of celestial phenomena. Although the hestiocentric system of Philolaus did not represent as great an advance toward a more accurate understanding of the universe as the geocentric model of the same period, it constituted a crucial step in the liberation of the human mind from the limitations of immediate sensory experience. In this sense, Pythagoras and Philolaus were the true precursors of the scientific revolution, anticipating by millennia the principle that underlying reality is mathematical, and that humanity can investigate it through mathematics.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
